  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Consider a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></math> efficient hydrogen-oxygen fuel cell working under standard conditions at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math> bar and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>298</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. Its cell reaction is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>The work derived from the cell on the consumption of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msup><mi>mol</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is used to compress <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>00</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></math> of a monoatomic ideal gas in a thermally insulated container. What is the change in the temperature (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> ) of the ideal gas?</p><p>The standard reduction potentials for the two half-cells are given below.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>23</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>00</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p>Use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>96500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>314</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "13.32",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>For given reaction&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mover><mo>&#10230;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></mrow></mover><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>23</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>&#916;G</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>nFE</mi><mtext>cell&#160;</mtext></msub><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>[</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>96500</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>23</mn><mo>]</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>166</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>173</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>166</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>173</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo>=</mo><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mi>nR&#916;T</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#947;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>166</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>173</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>314</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>&#916;T</mi></mrow><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>314</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>&#916;T</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;T</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>166</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>173</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>314</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>32</mn></math></p>"
